From: Macron <macron@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: Don't show the wait window while the prefix is
 updated.

wineboot shows "The Wine configuration in ... is being updated, please
wait..." while wine.inf is installed into a prefix: when the prefix is
made, when wine.inf is newer than the prefix's .update-timestamp, and on
wineboot -u. On a Mac the window turns the process into a Dock app with
Wine's name and icon, in front of the game that is starting, for the 15
to 40 seconds the update takes. Macron starts games through Steam and
does not want the player to see Wine. The update runs the same way,
without the window. MACRON_WINEBOOT_WAIT_WINDOW=1 shows it again, for a
check's control run.
---
diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
index 7dda9ec..19a1888 100644
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -1701,7 +1701,10 @@ static void update_wineprefix( BOOL force )
 
         if ((process = start_rundll32( inf_path, L"PreInstall", IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_TARGET_HOST )))
         {
-            HWND hwnd = show_wait_window();
+            /* Macron: no wait window. On a Mac it makes the process a Dock app named
+             * after Wine, in front of the game that is starting.
+             * MACRON_WINEBOOT_WAIT_WINDOW=1 brings it back (a check's control run). */
+            HWND hwnd = _wgetenv( L"MACRON_WINEBOOT_WAIT_WINDOW" ) ? show_wait_window() : 0;
             for (;;)
             {
                 if (process)
@@ -1722,7 +1725,7 @@ static void update_wineprefix( BOOL force )
                     process = start_rundll32( inf_path, L"Wow64Install", machines[count].Machine );
                 count++;
             }
-            DestroyWindow( hwnd );
+            if (hwnd) DestroyWindow( hwnd );
         }
         install_root_pnp_devices();
         update_user_profile();
